xt": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F2a7854da-71bf-4d53-953b-a4228a2a7bd4-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 208px; height: 194px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f18"}, {"id": "336bfe", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F997b603a-2286-4e8e-b920-79d7b18a2a41-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 208px; height: 194px;\" /></p>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f19"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f1a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b78a3a78c"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5674"], "concepts": ["61ab774f6fe44bfe0fe4966f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).</p><p><strong>Assertion (A):</strong> Ketoses give Seliwanoff&rsquo;s test faster than Aldoses.</p><p><strong>Reason (R):</strong> Ketoses undergo <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>-elimination followed by formation of furfural.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4d805d", "text": "(A) is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f1b"}, {"id": "145eda", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f1c"}, {"id": "558748", "text": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f1d"}, {"id": "1ee15c", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f1e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f822ee0e063d9292f1f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced5dd19d2aa2b